 "provenance": {
  "colour": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "The median of bare plate in the page 9 photographs is #1d1e20 on the front and #1d1e21 on the rear, a near black. Lettering on the rear is white; the front is lettered in a gold that is not drawn."
  },
  "ears": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "Estimated from the front view of the same drawing at 6.70 pixels to the millimetre. A flange stands 22.1 past each end of the 436 body and is 43 high, with two slotted holes. The front is therefore 480.2 wide and the chassis stays 436. The drawn front positions are the body's, shifted 22.1 to the right."
  },
  "front-layout": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "Every front position is read off the front view of the drawing on guide page 35 at 400 dpi (4.44 px/mm). The origin is the body's left edge, then each position is moved right by the ears. Each is checked against the labelled photograph on page 9. The drawing prints no dimension for any feature, so each is good to about 0.5 mm. The drawing also draws a SIM slot, three antenna connectors and a modem jack. The guide says the SIM slot and the modem apply to certain models and the R/U product page lists no cellular or modem feature, so none is drawn here."
  },
  "network": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "Guide page 11: \"two Ethernet combo pairs (RJ45 and SFP) identified as Ethernet 1 and 2\"; only one port of each pair is active at a time. The photograph shows an SFP cage above an RJ45 on each pair, numbered 1 and 2."
  },
  "power": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "Guide page 12: two inlets on the back, each with its own rocker switch. Guide page 27: \"100-240 VAC, 50-60 Hz, 1.5 Amps max\". The page: \"IEC320-C13 to NEMA 5-15P line cord\" and four other countries, so the inlet is a C14 (inferred from the cord end; the inlet's own type is not named). The R/U page prints 15.5 W typical and 47-63 Hz; the guide's 50-60 Hz is the one recorded."
  },
  "rear-layout": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "Every rear position is read off the labelled rear photograph of an SCG50 RRR-LAWM on guide page 9, 1278 px for the 436 mm body (2.93 px/mm across, 2.9 down). The photograph is slightly angled, so each position is estimated to within about 2 mm. The jack pitch reads 14.3 mm and the gap between modules 2.0 mm beyond one pitch; the registry's ganged-jack pitch of 13.97 does not fit the photograph's 24 columns. The two inlets, the rockers, the network cluster and the bays are placed the same way."
  },
  "serial-ports": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "Product page row: \"32 x RS232 RJ45\" is the model's own count (\"16 x RS232 RJ45 interfaces\" for the SCG18 R, per module). Guide page 27: \"shielded RJ45 ports\". Page 9 prints each column's two numbers as \"1^ 2v\" above it, odd above even. The ports are RS-232 with software selectable Cisco pinouts (the page)."
  },
  "sides": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "Estimated from the lower view of the drawing on guide page 35 at 600 dpi, 6.71 pixels to the millimetre (the 262 mm label). Each edge is good to about 0.3 mm. Both sides carry the ear bracket, six round holes and six slotted ovals. They also carry two rows of 32 vent slots, two more round holes and two ringed holes. The drawing does not say which side it shows. Its front is at the left, which is the right side on this library's views. So the right side is drawn as the drawing shows it, and the left is its mirror about the depth. The photograph of the unit on guide page 10 shows the same two vent rows in the middle of the side. It also shows a few small holes, in perspective. The photograph shows no bracket fitted, and the drawing draws one on each side in the ear's colour. The guide does not say how the brackets are supplied. The line colour and the hole colour are stand-ins on the body's near black."
  },
  "size": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "Guide page 35 (and the fixed-model guide, 5500438-10, page 20): the drawing's labels read 436MM, 44MM and 262MM, so the body is 436 wide, 44 high and 262 deep. The product page prints \"26.4 x 43.4 x 4.4 (cm)\", which differs by 2 mm in depth and width; the drawing is taken because it labels its axes. Height 44 against the 1U rack unit of 44.45 is the drawing's rounding. The drawing's front view is orthographic: 1935 px for the 436 mm body and 194 px for the face, 4.44 px/mm across and 4.44 down."
  },
  "sources": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "Perle, IOLAN SCG Hardware Installation Guide, Expandable Models (5500427-10, Sept 2021): page 7 (the unit, 1U), page 9 (labelled front and rear photographs of an SCG50 RRU-LAWM, RRR-LAWM and UUU-LAWM), page 10 (modules, the bays), pages 11 to 13 (network ports, inlets, power button), page 27 (specifications) and page 35 (Appendix D, the mechanical drawing). Perle, the IOLAN SCG R/U product page (the IOLAN SCG34 R row: description, part numbers, Specifications tab). No data sheet, CAD model or stencil is held."
  },
  "top-and-bottom": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "Estimated from the plan view of the same drawing. A line runs the full width 10.8 mm behind the front. The plan is not labelled top or bottom, so both faces carry it. The plan shows the bracket leg edge-on as a line about 2 mm outside each body edge, from 2.2 to 96.9 behind the front. The view is the 436 body, so the leg is drawn as a thin line on each edge, 94.7 long. The plan also shows the ear flange at each end of the front, about 2 mm deep and standing outside the body. Both faces stay the 436 mm body, and the flanges are not drawn on them. The drawing shows no vent or hole on the plan."
  }
